            <ArticleTitle>Closing radial wedge osteotomy for Preiser's disease: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1154-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of Preiser's disease treated with closing radial wedge osteotomy is reviewed and the therapeutic effect is reported. A good result was obtained in the short term and we believe that this surgical method could become one of the choices for surgical treatment to alleviate pain in Preiser's disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
